    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "3a6ea048_05f28d5e",
        "filename": "audio/effect/all-versions/vts/functional/Android.bp",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 34,
      "author": {
        "id": 1042638
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-12-13T17:43:50Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "My understanding is that due to \"vts-core\" it is possible to run these tests correctly in presubmit. Current issue with \"general-tests\" is that atest doesn\u0027t take into account \"binary-test-disable-framework\" and \"binary-test-stop-native-servers\" statements from the test xml config, and leaving framework and native servers running can interfere with VTS.",
      "parentUuid": "5d0c0ba7_965f1a23",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 34,
        "startChar": 18,
        "endLine": 34,
        "endChar": 33
      },
      "revId": "9d6c5163baa63882b1f8345d8bbe8d6aa5843663",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ba87c300_20892bcd",
        "filename": "audio/effect/all-versions/vts/functional/Android.bp",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 34,
      "author": {
        "id": 1088076
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-12-13T18:00:51Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "just to clarify, tests only need to be in general-tests or device-tests to be accessible by presubmit test run, e.g., through Test Mapping. Adding it to vts-core is for the test to be part of vts-core compliance suite (for OEM).\n\nThe missing \"binary-test-disable-framework\" option should be added to the test xml files in this CL.\nNote that it\u0027s a vts option. To be translated to TradeFed config:\n\"binary-test-disable-framework\" is equivalent to:\n\t\u003ctarget_preparer class\u003d\"com.android.tradefed.targetprep.RunCommandTargetPreparer\"\u003e\n\t\t\u003coption name\u003d\"run-command\" value\u003d\"stop\"/\u003e\n\t\t\u003coption name\u003d\"teardown-command\" value\u003d\"start\"/\u003e\n\t\u003c/target_preparer\u003e\n\n\"binary-test-stop-native-servers\" is only related to vts harness (\"vts.native_server.on\" system property). Since the test will be a generic native test that doesn\u0027t require vts harness, the option is no longer needed.",
      "parentUuid": "3a6ea048_05f28d5e",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 34,
        "startChar": 18,
        "endLine": 34,
        "endChar": 33
      },
      "revId": "9d6c5163baa63882b1f8345d8bbe8d6aa5843663",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "3ccc8133_588bf4cf",
        "filename": "audio/effect/all-versions/vts/functional/Android.bp",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 34,
      "author": {
        "id": 1042638
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-12-13T18:19:43Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thanks Dan!\n\nAnd is an equivalent for \"binary-test-stop-native-servers\"? In practice, this results in issuing the following command: \"adb shell setprop vts.native_server.on 1\"\n\nNelson, could you please add these commands to the XML files? I know that effects tests usually pass even if you don\u0027t satisfy these conditions, but depending on the framework activity they might fail.",
      "parentUuid": "ba87c300_20892bcd",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 34,
        "startChar": 18,
        "endLine": 34,
        "endChar": 33
      },
      "revId": "9d6c5163baa63882b1f8345d8bbe8d6aa5843663",
